{"timestamp":"2026-11-08T19:59:39.450Z","ordinal":47671,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1b054-fe0d-76c1-a45c-4726d155f0fa","turn_id":"01a1b8a7-3fc8-7460-a590-a3bb58793d59","item":{"type":"McpToolCall","id":"exec-fda6e7e1-783d-4870-aa9b-76b00dd7cc71","server":"english-pilot","tool":"english_coaching_context","arguments":{},"status":"completed","result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"guidance\": \"Do not derail the user's main task. Enforce mode is enabled: over-threshold prompts are handled by the submit hook before the agent turn. Force mode is enabled: append one English note using the configured note depth whenever the prompt has Chinese fragments, non-native phrasing, or a clearly better everyday expression. Prefer practical workplace English, brief teaching rationale, and reusable expressions.\",\n  \"finalResponseInstruction\": \"Finish the main task first. For the latest allowed user prompt, append one English note using the configured note depth if it contains any Chinese fragment, awkward English, or obvious phrasing improvement: Use a Rich English Note by default: 5-8 useful lines, brief enough for a final response but rich enough for study.\\nUse this shape:\\nEnglish note:\\nOriginal: \\\"fix this problem\\\"\\nBetter: \\\"fix this issue\\\" / \\\"resolve this startup issue\\\"\\nWhy: In engineering conversations, \\\"issue\\\" is more precise than \\\"problem\\\" when discussing bugs, failures, tickets, or startup errors.\\nUseful patterns:\\n- \\\"The MCP client failed during the startup handshake.\\\"\\n- \\\"This issue belongs at the config boundary, not the runtime path.\\\"\\nCollocations: startup issue, handshake failure, config mismatch, reproduce the issue, verify the fix\\nCommon mistake: Use \\\"problem\\\" for general trouble; use \\\"issue\\\" for bugs, tickets, incidents, and engineering discussions.\\nIPA: issue /ˈɪʃuː/ or /ˈɪsjuː/ For programming-task conversations, prefer software-engineering English in the final note. Good sentence patterns: append an English note at the end; keep the behavior behind a small interface; make the failure path explicit; cache the result to avoid repeating the same expensive operation; this change belongs at the module boundary. Use the configured computer-English files as vocabulary hints, not as text to quote every time.\",\n  \"domainReference\": {\n    \"style\": \"software-engineering\",\n    \"available\": false,\n    \"terms\": [],\n    \"examples\": [\n      \"append an English note at the end\",\n      \"keep the behavior behind a small interface\",\n      \"make the failure path explicit\",\n      \"cache the result to avoid repeating the same expensive operation\",\n      \"this change belongs at the module boundary\"\n    ],\n    \"missingPaths\": []\n  },\n  \"cadence\": \"Force mode bypasses cooldown and daily-cap intent for teachable user prompts; follow the configured note depth and keep the note professional. Skip only when there is no meaningful wording improvement.\",\n  \"policy\": {\n    \"gateMode\": \"enforce\",\n    \"intensity\": \"force\",\n    \"cooldownMinutes\": 0,\n    \"maxInlineCoachingPerDay\": 999,\n    \"assistantEnglishNoteDepth\": \"rich\"\n  },\n  \"today\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-08\",\n    \"coachingShown\": 0,\n    \"remaining\": 999\n  },\n  \"cooldown\": {\n    \"active\": false,\n    \"lastShownAt\": \"2026-08-01T13:52:28.084Z\"\n  },\n  \"decision\": {\n    \"shouldOfferInlineCoaching\": true,\n    \"reason\": \"available\"\n  }\n}"}]},"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":980427875}},"started_at_ms":1794167978469,"completed_at_ms":1794167979450}}
